 ## 1 · Rulings (spec seat, 2026-11-09)
 
 - **R-1, the mechanism: the shared silhouette with the lens under the ink.** Each member keeps its own lens, a `backdrop-filter` that spans the cluster box and is clipped to that member's share of one silhouette (B's geometry). Every lens paints before any ink, so no lens samples a neighbour's veil. The ink is a member GlassDock's own `.dock-plate`: its ink tier, earned darken and grain stay GlassDock's, and only its shape changes. One rim and one shadow are drawn from the whole silhouette.
