 - **The shape** is `dockClusterShape.ts`, B's module generalised to the member's corner (R-4). Each join runs in two phases: for j ≤ 0.4 the facing ends bulge to contact at the cut, and past 0.4 the waist opens with `v = √((j − 0.4)/0.6)`. Every value is in px, every cut snaps to a device pixel in page space, and shares of unequal height meet at the mean.
-- **The springs** are one `useDockSpring(DOCK_SPRING)` per join, where `DOCK_SPRING` is `springPreset("dock")` (R-11). Each join springs from its painted value to its target; an interruption re-plays only the joins whose target changed, each carrying its own velocity. A width glide adds two (one per edge), a run (an arriver or a leaver's phantom) one, and a pure leave one per moving survivor (R-7). A change to a live spring's target is a retarget (R-7, R-11).
